center. (C) Mature nacre. (D and E) Atomic-resolution image of atoms in nacre. (F) Transition from spherulitic aragonite structures to nacre. (G and H) Aggregated nanoparticles form massive aragonite. (I) The formation of nacre begins directly on massive aragonite.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APearlCrossSection_Figure1.pdf"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Two_halved_river_pearls%2C_natural_freshwater_pearls_on_lapis_lazuli.jpg/500px-Two_halved_river_pearls%2C_natural_freshwater_pearls_on_lapis_lazuli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Two_halved_river_pearls%2C_natural_freshwater_pearls_on_lapis_lazuli.jpg/500px-Two_halved_river_pearls%2C_natural_freshwater_pearls_on_lapis_lazuli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two halved river pearls, natural freshwater pearls, on a slab of lapis lazuli. The pearls are about 2.5–3 mm (0.098–0.118 in) in diameter. The growth layers are clearly visible.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATwo_halved_river_pearls%2C_natural_freshwater_pearls_on_lapis_lazuli.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Pearls.jpg/500px-Pearls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Pearls.jpg/500px-Pearls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nuclei from Mikimoto Pearl Island, Toba, Japan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APearls.jpg"}],"sounds":{"midnight":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/En-us-midnight.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/36/En-us-midnight.ogg/En-